Our index.html currently has placeholder startLoop that cancel previous loop and requestAnimationFrame tick, but tick currently only calculates dt and requestAnimationFrame(tick), without clearing canvas, update/render calls. We need to implement startLoop to cancel previous loop, set loopId null and schedule tick with requestAnimationFrame. The tick should compute dt, call update(dt) and render(), then publishState() (the observable contract). Must wrap the body in try/catch. Also need to clear canvas each frame (or we do in render anyway). Actually the spec for animation loop: "clears canvas each frame, wraps update/render calls in try/catch". In render we probably clear canvas.

But we haven't defined update, render functions yet. Must they be stubbed? The spec says implement startLoop that cancels previous loop, uses requestAnimationFrame, clears canvas each frame, wraps update/render calls in try/catch.

We could call clearRect before update? Actually typical: tick -> clear canvas -> update -> render.

Let's implement:

function startLoop() {
  if (loopId !== null) cancelAnimationFrame(loopId);
  const canvas = document.getElementById('game');
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
  function tick(now) {
    const dt = Math.min((now - lastTime) / 1000, 0.1);
    lastTime = now;
    try {
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
      // update and render if functions exist
      if (typeof update === 'function') update(dt);
      if (typeof render === 'function') render();
      // publishState if defined
      if (typeof publishState === 'function') publishState();
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('loop error', err);
    }
    loopId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }
  loopId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
}

